From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:13:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 67/90] Deliver EE SIF commands through registered IOP handlers

Honor user/system handler tables and registration GP without using their memory for packets. Parse public/internal EE argument-register ABIs, transfer extra payload to IOP RAM, and allow SIF replies to interrupt HLE guest callbacks.

Regressions cover command delivery, table canaries, packet reclamation, removal/reset, both EE entry points and a reply followed by IRQ during an HLE callback. ABI and nesting regressions fail before their fixes; full tests pass afterward.

